      "value": "If this were accepted as valid, the system would hallucinate structure from noise — treating unstructured arrays as evidence. In reality, without labeled axes, units, or purpose, these numbers are meaningless for validation. A correct output would specify which values correspond to what metric (e.g., val_err, test_loss), compare them against thresholds (e.g., ≤1e-3), and justify conclusions via iteration history or physical constraints."
